SM(564,{"n":"2 Corinthians 6","a":"Fr Stephen De Young Archives/2 Corinthians 6.mp3","d":2886.5,"s":[[0.16,"Come and study holy scriptures with us as Father Stephen DeYoung teaches verse by verse on the podcast The Whole Counsel of God."],[8.08,"Father Stephen is a former Protestant pastor and Bible teacher in the Reformed Church, but now an Orthodox priest serving at Archangel Gabriel Orthodox Church in Lafayette, Louisiana."],[20.88,"We'll go ahead and uh get started."],[23.52,"And when we get started, we're going to be picking up at the beginning of St."],[28.24,"Paul's Second Epistle to the Corinthians, uh, chapter six."],[32.8,"Um, and uh just by quick quick catch-up, um, because now we've gone through this several times."],[42.24,"Um, St. Paul is this is actually, at least his fourth letter that he's written to the church at Corinth."],[50.16,"Um this uh letter that we're reading at Second Corinthians is probably, as we also mentioned, made up of more than one letter that's been put together."],[59.44,"But uh this is being written after a visit from Saint Paul and then another letter that did not go so well."],[68.12,"Um Corinth is still having a lot of problems."],[71.24,"He's been trying to work with them to resolve those problems, and and things got very messy."],[76.68,"And so we've seen that um one of, if not the main theme that St."],[82.76,"Paul is getting at in this letter is trying to talk to them about reconciliation."],[87.4,"Uh primarily being reconciled with each other."],[89.88,"He's said over and over again that he's he it's not that he's mad or upset at anyone or offended at anyone, um, but that they need to be reconciled to one another and come back together uh as one as one church."],[104.52,"And that's actually been his main focus"],[108.48,"Uh, last time, as we went through uh chapter five, we saw how Saint Paul uh was talking to them."],[117.6,"He's really further developing some themes that we saw in 1 Corinthians, both in terms of spiritual gifts and abilities and capacities that God has given us, and then the reality of uh Christ's return and the last judgment, and that we're gonna be held accountable for sort of how we used those faculties and abilities and gifts uh that God has given us uh in this world."],[141.44,"And so with those abilities and gifts comes a sort of accountability and responsibility for what we do with them. them and how we use"],[153.24,"So that's really, I know that was short, but that really is where we're about to pick up."],[158.44,"So unless there are any comments or questions or rumors or superstitions that anyone wants to share, we'll go ahead and get started in St."],[174.92,"Paul's second epistle to the Corinthians, chapter 6, verse 1."],[181.96,"We then, as workers together with Him, also plead with you not to receive the grace of God in vain."],[190.2,"So this is this is an important verse, maybe more important than it looks like. at first"],[197.52,"But uh the reason it's so important uh is real really has to do with sort of our modern situation as as Christians."],[209.04,"Um and um sort of the the some of the beliefs and teachings of some of our uh Protestant Christian friends um that are kind of contradicted by uh this verse."],[224.32,"And it may not be obvious how that is."],[227.74,"Um but uh we'll take a look at it a little more closely."],[231.18,"So he says, we then, as workers together with him."],[236.26,"Okay. The word that's translated workers together there is one word"],[244.68,"It's sinery. Which is where the word like synergy or synergism in English comes from."],[257.93,"And the verse continues."],[261.39,"We're co-workers with him, with God."],[265.07,"And you'll notice that's in italics, that with him is added."],[268.93,"But if you're if you're co-workers, you have to be co-workers with someone else."],[273.75,"And go if you go back to the previous verse."],[278.33,"It's talking about Christ."],[280.38,"The previous section."],[281.94,"So if you're talking about Christ, and then you say, we as co-workers."],[288.36,"Then obviously the person who you're co-workers with is Christ."],[296.17,"And so he pleads not to receive the grace of God in vain."],[302.09,"And that second part is also important."],[305.29,"Because if St."],[306.73,"Paul is pleading with the people in Corinth not to receive the grace of God in vain, that means it's possible to receive the grace of God in vain."],[318.83,"I mean, that would seem just obvious."],[320.91,"Our Calvinist friends deny that that is possible"],[321.11,"Okay. One of their basic teachings is irresistible grace."],[332.81,"And they will say that grace is monergistic."],[337.46,"Just one person working, just God does it."],[342.19,"God saves you by his grace, and when he does it, you're not doing anything."],[347.79,"St. Paul here just used the word sinery."],[352.45,"Just use the words for synergism."],[355.35,"Which is not monergism."],[356.73,"Synergism means working together."],[359.94,"And said that that's necessary, or we will receive the grace of God in vain."],[365.06,"Okay Now, someone could say, well, this is this isn't talking about grace like salvation."],[375.92,"They could say, well, you know, there's just common grace from God."],[380.62,"He makes us alive."],[382.24,"Whether we're we're wicked or evil, whether we're faithful or unfaithful."],[386.98,"He gives us this life, he gives us good things."],[389.86,"So you could say, well, St."],[391.06,"Paul's just talking about that."],[393.07,"But you're going to have to work on that."],[394.59,"Except, well, and except verse 21 of chapter 5, the verse right before this."],[404.84,"For he made him who knew no sin to be. sin for us, that we might become the righteousness of God in him"],[412.16,"That's talking about Christ, his death and resurrection."],[415.7,"That's talking about our salvation."],[418.5,"So St. Paul didn't just change topics."],[422.12,"I mean, we've got this big number six."],[424.78,"But that's not there in the original."],[428.62,"This is the next just the next sentence with no break in what St."],[433.74,"Paul wrote. So you put the six and I'm awesome."],[436.62,"So but so what what grace is this?"],[439.26,"It's the grace he was just talking about."],[443.43,"He says, this is what God did."],[446.85,"Now we as co-workers with God, in this matter, urge you not to receive the grace of God in vain."],[459.13,"God has given you this grace."],[460.33,"He did this."],[461.07,"Christ's already done it."],[462.27,"He did it a couple thousand years before I was born."],[465.55,"Okay? So he did it."],[468.56,"And I receive the benefits of what Christ did by grace."],[474.32,"But if I don't cooperate, that's the Latin version."],[478.74,"Co, like soon, like together."],[481.44,"Operate, like ergo, right write, work, oper."],[485.1,"If I don't cooperate with that grace, then I will. receive it in vain"],[494.16,"And and the word for vain here is empty."],[496.65,"It's like it's empty, it comes to nothing."],[501.59,"It doesn't actually do anything."],[505.11,"Okay. And so this is this is important in understanding Saint Paul's whole theology."],[511.72,"We talked about this back when we talked about Romans."],[513.88,"That was a long time ago now."],[515.66,"More than a year ago, I think."],[519.1,"Well, you can still listen to it on ancient faith."],[521.42,"Um, but uh Saint Paul is very clear, that Christ has done what he has done."],[532.21,"We didn't do anything to get Christ to die for us."],[537.79,"It's and he was countering right the view of the Pharisees in his day, and remember Saint Paul was one, was well, we got into this mess by disobeying the Torah."],[549.57,"So if we could just obey the Torah perfectly, then God will send the Messiah and sort of rescue us from this bad situation."],[557.35,"God will God will return to us."],[558.87,"And he was countering that."],[559.75,"He was saying, no, Christ did it, and he did it, as he says in Romans, at just the right time while we were still sinners."],[567.4,"While we were still out there sinning and rebelling, God acted."],[573.21,"And that's what Saint Paul would tell us we should expect, because that's what happened in Exodus."],[582.31,"It's not that the Israelites were slaves, and they all started obeying the law of God perfectly, and so God rescued them from slavery."],[593.05,"And gave them the land."],[594.25,"Like they earned it."],[596.14,"Not at all."],[597.35,"They were sinful and wicked."],[598.55,"They were honored all through the desert."],[600.23,"Most of them died in the desert."],[601.57,"And all that."],[602.98,"God did it."],[603.78,"So St. Paul's very clear about that."],[606.36,"Christ came and defeated death, defeated the devil."],[610.17,"That's um uh purified the world from sin."],[614.01,"He did all those things"],[614.09,"He did. just them before any of us were born"],[621.65,"He's also clear, however, that for that to be meaningful for us, that there is this cooperation required."],[634.42,"Again, not where we like earn something."],[637.96,"But where God is doing something in us and through us, and we cooperate with it instead of resisting and rebelling against it."],[648.73,"Because that's what the Israelites did in the wilderness."],[652.11,"The ones who died in the desert."],[655.47,"Rather than cooperating with God and following God through the desert to the promised land that he was giving them."],[662.25,"They resisted and rebelled and grumbled and criticized and went after Moses and said, We had it better in Egypt."],[669.45,"And yeah, on and on and on and on and on."],[672.38,"And so they ended up destroying themselves because they resisted."],[676.84,"God still brought them out of Egypt."],[680.6,"So they received the grace of God."],[682.44,"They were set free from slavery."],[684.94,"They received those, but it amounted to nothing."],[687.98,"Because they resisted it and they rebelled against it."],[691.84,"So for them, it it it amounted, it amounted to nothing."],[695.44,"And so St."],[696.56,"Paul is talking about the same kind of dynamic possible for us today."],[702.54,"For the Corinthians then, the people of the Church of Corinth."],[706.42,"They've been baptized."],[708.84,"As Saint Paul went through in 1 Corinthians."],[711.42,"Just like just like all those people had been baptized into Moses in the Red Sea and in the cloud and went into the wilderness."],[718.32,"All the people in Corinth have been baptized."],[720.82,"They've received the Holy Spirit, they're they're in the church, they're hearing the word of God."],[726.43,"All these things."],[728.56,"But there's still this possibility that if they harden their hearts like those Israelites did in the wilderness, that they won't end up making it out of the wilderness into the promised land."],[739.36,"So the once they always say you' justre all the window."],[742.68,"Well, yeah. St."],[744.6,"Paul certainly never says that."],[748.41,"And so that's that's what he's talking about again here."],[752.19,"And this is also important that he's clarifying it here."],[757.15,"Because remember, he's just been telling them, God's given you these abilities, these gifts, these powers, these capabilities."],[763.71,"He's going to judge you based on how you use them."],[767.57,"But he's now making clear that he's not talking about like, well, okay, God's g gonnaonna, God's like a referee."],[776.66,"It's up to you to work out your salvation, and then God will sort of give you a grade."],[782.56,"At the end of it."],[783.64,"That's not how it works either."],[785.77,"So he says, if you're if you're doing the right thing, if you're using those gifts that God has given you, those capabilities he's given you in the right way to do good."],[796.25,"What you're you're you're not doing that sort of independently, you're doing that by cooperating with what God is doing."],[808.25,"So this is this is really important, and this is this is um a crucial part of the way the Orthodox Church understands good works."],[822.61,"Um if you're familiar at all with debates between roman catholic folks and protestant folks you know that everybody gets better right is it just faith is it faith and works what are good works how does that work and merit and all these things okay so in in in the understanding of the orthodox church right grace is is the energies of god and energies i know we hear it and we think mwom woman right that's that's not that's that's not what what the term uh we've sci fi is kind of ruined that word for us."],[864.07,"Um but the n is in and erg again is like in synergy, it's working."],[870.09,"So it's God working working in his creation, God working in and through his creation, and God is continually in and through his creation to bring it to perfection."],[881.15,"To transfigure it, to transform it, continuously."],[892.13,"We either become co-workers with him, in terms of both ourselves and the world around us."],[899.15,"Or we rebel and resist what he's doing."],[904.19,"And the big problem is if we rebel and resist what he's doing, not only does that make us not a part of it."],[912.52,"But it doesn't stop him from getting it done."],[917.1,"We just end up destroying ourselves."],[919.92,"We opt out of it."],[923.45,"We're removed from it."],[925.37,"And that's why you have all of this imagery in um regarding the people who end up being condemned at the last judgment of being sort of outside."],[938.19,"Outside the kingdom or shut out."],[940.77,"Or in this dark place outside, because they've opted out."],[945.55,"God is doing something here, they haven't wanted to be a part of it, and they've removed themselves from it."],[952.8,"Um, so so we we participate in it, okay?"],[958.56,"And so here's an analogy."],[962.09,"And like all analogies, it's not perfect, okay, but uh here's an analogy."],[968.57,"If I'm going to buy a house, I'm going to use a realtor."],[976.46,"And I'm going to send that realtor to go and negotiate the price."],[981.44,"Make offers. Do all the actual stuff, signing papers involved in buying a house."],[991.19,"So who buys the house?"],[994.07,"the house I'm by I'm the one buying."],[1000.22,"I'm paying the money and I'm receiving the house."],[1004.86,"Okay. But all of the actions involved in buying the house, who's doing those?"],[1012.38,"The realtor. The realtor."],[1017.92,"So again, this is an analogy."],[1021.25,"So when God, St."],[1023.73,"Paul's gonna say elsewhere, God has good works prepared in advance for us to do."],[1029.22,"God is working in his creation."],[1032.42,"When we offer ourselves, we talked about this already with prayer."],[1035.79,"When we offer ourselves to God to be his his instruments, to do will, we can look at that the same way."],[1046.08,"Who does the actual actions?"],[1048.0,"Who's the person who goes."],[1050.26,"Well will use the church service."],[1051.86,"Who's the person who actually walks up to the altar and preaches the sermon and breaks the bread and pours the wine?"],[1061.39,"I'm the one who does all those actions."],[1063.79,"Yeah. But who's the one who's communicating himself to the people?"],[1070.25,"Christ. So if you go and talk to someone about the gospel, who's the person talking?"],[1077.63,"You If that person finds salvation, did you save them?"],[1086.61,"No, Christ saved them."],[1090.69,"You had the privilege of being the one who he did that through, but he did it."],[1097.81,"You can't take credit for it."],[1100.51,"My realtor can't show up and say, I bought five houses today."],[1103.63,"They say, really?"],[1104.27,"You own five houses?"],[1105.23,"Well, no, I don't own any of them."],[1109.58,"Even though they're the ones who perform the actions."],[1113.1,"But here's the other reason why the realtor is a good metaphor."],[1116.86,"Because the realtor does derive benefit from having been the person who did it."],[1125.27,"I mean, they get a commission."],[1126.87,"Oh, yeah. I mean, that's how they make a living, is by being the person who does that."],[1131.28,"And so, in the same way, when we're participating and cooperating with what God is doing in the world, we benefit from that."],[1139.52,"We're transformed by that."],[1141.2,"We're changed by that."],[1143.86,"That's part of how we find our salvation."],[1148.56,"Is by participating it."],[1150.16,"But even those benefits that we get, just like the realtor's commission comes from me."],[1157.17,"Those changes in us come from God too."],[1160.69,"So God is changing us."],[1161.81,"ing God is accomplishing what he's do."],[1161.89,"And that's why God can look at those works and call them good"],[1169.05,"Because they're his."],[1170.49,"They're not mine."],[1172.65,"He's not going to look at anything I do and call it good."],[1175.87,"At least not in the sense of perfect."],[1178.56,"But he looks at his own works just like on the days of creation."],[1181.6,"He gets done creating, he looks at it and he says, it's good, because he did it."],[1185.74,"And so he can look at the work at the end and say it's good."],[1188.46,"It could be a good work because it's his work."],[1195.23,"Done through me."],[1196.27,"And if I had refused, he would have done it some other way."],[1201.39,"It still would have been accomplished by him, but I would have lost out on that benefit."],[1204.59,"I wouldn't have been a part on it of it"],[1211.59,"So my choice, doesn't earn anything."],[1217.23,"It's just whether or not I exclude myself from God's grace."],[1226.83,"And so that's that's really what St."],[1230.19,"Paul has been teaching."],[1231.15,"We, I mean, we we started talking about this with prayer back a few chapters."],[1237.0,"And this is one of St."],[1239.0,"Paul's themes all the way through these chapters."],[1242.26,"Is that this is what the people in Corinth need to do and and how they need to look at it."],[1247.22,"God is doing these things."],[1248.86,"He's doing these things in you and in your community and in the world."],[1252.62,"You need to be a part of it."],[1255.1,"You need to be reconciled to him and to each other so you can be a part of it."],[1260.54,"Because if you resist, if you resist each other, if you resist being reconciled to each other, if you resist God, you're not going to be a part of it."],[1267.74,"You're going to be cut off."],[1269.5,"And then the grace you've already received isn't going to come to anything."],[1274.7,"Because you're rejecting it and cutting yourself off from it."],[1279.58,"This is inspiring because it gives significance to our actions without giving us a reason to be boastful."],[1288.44,"We have nothing to brag about, but our actions are incredibly significant."],[1292.2,"Yeah And that's a gift that God gives us."],[1299.97,"When God calls us to be the one who does these things, he's offering us a gift that we can accept or refuse."],[1308.87,"And so this is also the flip side."],[1310.96,"When St. Paul says be reconciled, on one side, there's you've got to be willing to forgive these people when they return."],[1319.76,"On the other side, these people have to be willing to return."],[1324.24,"They have to be willing to be reconciled."],[1328.88,"And not harden their hearts and say, well, you know, that community was mean to to me me when they had discipline, so I'm not going back."],[1335.28,"So I'm done"],[1340.34,"How dare they talk to me that way?"],[1342.1,"Or whatever. And so both sides are important."],[1346.36,"And so that's why St."],[1347.32,"Paul is emphasizing this."],[1348.6,"He's saying to those people who are now separated from the community, you need to come back."],[1355.72,"While he's also said to the people still in the community, you need to receive them back."],[1362.44,"Because if you don't come back, you're just going to keep cutting yourself off from what God is doing and wants to do in and through you as a person and as a community."],[1375.52,"Does so its seem like this is something he comes back to?"],[1382.32,"This is a big deal."],[1384.24,"But does he ever address how to recognize your ignorance if you frustrate the grace of God?"],[1394.24,"When how do you recognize that early?"],[1397.92,"Does he ever talk about that?"],[1400.24,"Yeah, he's gonna come back to it on what that practically means."],[1404.56,"But yeah, he's but he's also making the point it's never sort of too late."],[1408.74,"You may have hardened your heart for three years and said, I'll never go back, I'm done with it for right, but tomorrow you can soften it."],[1419.03,"And and come back."],[1420.63,"But if I understand your question, you're asking how can we recognize that we are frustrating a little God or not?"],[1422.87,"Yeah Yeah. And he's gonna he's gonna come back to this some more as we kind of similar."],[1434.75,"Yes, sir. Um how do we know what God was doing and how we can participate in?"],[1441.79,"Yeah. Yeah, he's gonna talk more about that, but I'll go into that a little."],[1449.39,"Um, I mean, the f the first way is that um the gospel itself is the proclamation of what God is doing."],[1459.41,"And so, for example, what St."],[1460.85,"Paul just said in the previous verse about Christ who knew no sin becoming sin for us that we might become the righteousness of God."],[1469.83,"Everything he just said is what God is doing."],[1476.89,"God is in Christ reconciling the whole world to himself."],[1479.53,"So there's something he's doing."],[1481.99,"When he talks in 1 Corinthians 13 about love."],[1486.32,"He talks about how the love of God, is coming to us and how we, by loving one another, participate and cooperate with the love of God."],[1498.78,"Because, you know, my love is human and fragile and tainted with sin."],[1503.92,"But if I become the way that God loves you, if God's loving you through me, if you're experiencing the love of God through me being kind to you, then that love is perfect and good because it's God's love."],[1519.16,"Not mine. And by me being the one who shows that to you again, I'm transformed and changed by the love of God in the process."],[1527.88,"And that's all of those things that uh in St."],[1530.92,"Matthew's gospel are the like visiting the sick and people in prison, and all of those."],[1537.24,"Those are the things that express God's love to other people."],[1541.38,"So that's yeah, that's how that's how Saint Paul understands the commandments and the law, the Torah."],[1552.12,"Um He repeats what the Torah itself says, that he who does these things will find life in them."],[1560.77,"That the commandments bring life."],[1562.29,"How do the commandments bring life?"],[1564.29,"Well, the commandments are our guide, to what God is doing in the world."],[1571.94,"They're our guide to his will in the world."],[1574.6,"And so by following them, we're participating."],[1577.82,"So when God says in Leviticus, love your neighbor as yourself, when you do that, then you're a part of what God is doing in the world, and that's transformative."],[1589.13,"And gives you life."],[1591.15,"That's why how you find life in the commandments."],[1596.63,"So all of those, all of those commandments, he's going to talk about in a little bit here, seconds, he's going to talk about holiness."],[1606.93,"And a whole bunch of the commandments are about being holy."],[1610.43,"About are about staying away from things that are filthy and unclean and being separate, from those things and maintaining purity."],[1619.18,"That's a big focus, of the commandments."],[1621.78,"And so God is holy."],[1624.84,"And God is making his creation holy by purifying it."],[1630.9,"And and and making it sacred."],[1632.82,"And so when we participate in that, again, we find we find life in that"],[1640.38,"Right? So all of the commandments of Scripture, Old and New Testament, when properly understood, are a guide to that."],[1650.19,"They're a guide to God's will and what God is doing, in His in His creation."],[1657.81,"And it's important to distinguish that from the way a lot of times we in the contemporary world talk about figuring out God's will."],[1666.45,"Because a lot of times when we talk about figuring out God's will, it's we have to make some particular decision, like should should should I marry this person or not I do this career or not right and we and we want to figure out what God's what God's will is right and the both good and bad news right is that unless there's something sinful about it right like if your career choice is like running a brothel or a casino right then we would say well no that's not right God's will because we have the commandments to know that right but if you're if your career is you know should I become a carpenter or a plumber right like you get to to choose choose I say that's both good and bad news because it's good news in the sense that you get it's bad news in the sense that you have to choose you can't like throw the Urim and Thumum and sort of opt out of the opt out of the decision right um so yeah so that there's there's just wisdom now there's there's wisdom involved in making those kinds of decisions in the sense that we don't always know all the ramifications so we would say, well, yeah, there's nothing innately sinful about being a lawyer, for example."],[1759.77,"But there are types of law and things that you could legally do as a lawyer that would still be sinful."],[1768.43,"And that a Christian couldn't and shouldn't do."],[1770.92,"And so there's wisdom involved in being able to assess that situation and say, well, you know, at this time in this jurisdiction, maybe I can be a lawyer, but I can't be this type of lawyer."],[1781.4,"Or I can't work at this office, or I can't work for this person."],[1785.82,"So there's there's wisdom involved there in understanding all of those things."],[1792.94,"But yeah, it's uh God doesn't have a will, contrary to some of our extreme Calvinist friends, God doesn't have a will that includes what cereal you should eat in the morning."],[1808.87,"And whether you should have apple jacks or or uh sugar crisp, you know."],[1815.37,"Um He doesn't have this sort of you know minutiae, and somehow if you do the wrong thing, you're in trouble."],[1822.43,"Yeah. Sorry. Very little decision."],[1825.87,"Yeah, God's will is about what he's doing in the world."],[1829.92,"There's a direct connection between God's will and his energies."],[1833.6,"But whether you're a plumber or a carpenter, you're supposed to be kind to the poor and show love to people."],[1843.34,"All the fruits of the spirit."],[1844.56,"Love, joy, peace, patience, kindness, goodness, all those things, no matter what your your job is."],[1850.72,"That could be hard to do when no one else around you is doing that."],[1852.48,"And that's exactly the problem they were having in Corinth"],[1854.04,"That's absolutely true."],[1855.48,"Yes. Where they were surrounded by pagans."],[1863.4,"That's the problem we have when we're surrounded by pagans."],[1867.64,"Yeah. And so they had to they were to some extent, or they should have been."],[1873.74,"Part of the problem is that they weren't."],[1875.26,"Part of the problem is that they were basically living like pagans 85 to 90% of the time, and then trying to live like Christians, the other 10 or fifteen."],[1884.78,"And even bringing some of that paganism with them when they went to went to the church."],[1890.34,"Um, that was the big problem in 1 Corinthians."],[1893.88,"And so, yeah, that's why it' it'ss such such a problem there is that St."],[1896.2,"a Paul is having to really draw these lines and say, no, to certain extent, to a greater extent than we would have to today, at least for now, who knows where the future's gonna go."],[1910.88,"But um, at least for now, to a much greater extent than us, they had to opt out of everything."],[1917.04,"I mean, the feast days of the city were all worship of the pagan gods, and they couldn't participate."],[1924.09,"The the guilds in ancient Greek cities."],[1928.03,"So the craftsmen's guilds and those kind of things all had patron gods, and a major part of their meetings was worship of the patron gods of their guild."],[1938.91,"Well. if you're a Christian, you're gonna have to opt out"],[1945.91,"And if you're not part of the guild, that's gonna make things very, very difficult."],[1951.59,"But so yeah, that's that's a big part of what he's having to deal with with them, is that you know, as hard as it is, and that's part of the reason why St."],[1962.15,"Paul, he's not bragging."],[1963.93,"But why St."],[1964.73,"Paul repeatedly, when he's writing to the church in Corinth, talks about all the things he's suffered, all the shipwrecks and the beatings, and the thing."],[1972.13,"He's like, because he he knows."],[1974.59,"I mean, he's going around preaching the gospel, he's been rejected and hated and you know, thrown in pa prison, and all those things have happened to him."],[1981.95,"So it's not like he doesn't know, it's not like he's asking him to do this thinging and he doesn't know how hard it is, or he doesn't know what he's ask them to give up or sacrifice."],[1984.67,"He knows And he knows it's hard, but it's still what they need to ultimately do."],[1996.69,"Because just how bad influence works, so does good influence."],[2000.29,"Yeah. Yeah. Yeah."],[2003.81,"Which is why in uh 1 Corinthians he quoted uh Menander, uh the uh Greek uh comedic playwright who said, Bad company corrupts good morals."],[2021.73,"So much for verse one."],[2026.33,"Okay. verse Let's go to two."],[2029.33,"Yeah, yeah Oh, charging ahead."],[2034.81,"I know we're barreling through this passage."],[2037.37,"In fact, looking looking at the timer, that may have just been an episode all by itself."],[2042.41,"But we'll see."],[2044.25,"So uh chapter six, verse two."],[2049.13,"For he says, In an acceptable time I have heard you, and in the day of salvation I have helped you."],[2054.81,"Behold, now is the accepted time."],[2057.21,"Behold, now is the day of salvation."],[2060.94,"So St. Paul quotes Isaiah."],[2063.5,"In Isaiah, it was prophetic."],[2066.32,"That the where God is saying, the time is gonna come."],[2069.62,"When he's gonna act."],[2071.9,"To save his people"],[2072.1,"Paul is saying, guess what"],[2074.32,"St. That's now."],[2079.06,"That's now. And that that gets into what we were just saying."],[2083.73,"No matter how long you've hardened your heart."],[2086.15,"No matter how long you've been resisting God and what he's doing, no matter what, what."],[2092.6,"Today. Now's the time."],[2094.94,"So you can find salvation right now, today."],[2097.74,"It's still now for us."],[2099.34,"Yeah. Yeah. So got God has done it in Christ."],[2104.87,"It's happened. So you just need to be reconciled."],[2111.99,"We give no offense in anything that our ministry may not be blamed, but in all things we commend ourselves as ministers of God, in much patience, in tribulations and needs and distresses, and stripes and imprisonments, in tumults, in labors and sleeplessness and fastings, by purity, by knowledge, by long suffering, by kindness, by the Holy Spirit, by sincere love, by the word of truth, by the power of God, by the armor of righteousness on the right hand and on the left, by honor and dishonor, by evil report and good report, as deceivers and yet true, as unknown and yet well known, as dying and behold we live, as chastened and yet not killed, as sorrowful yet always rejoicing, as poor yet making many. rich, as having nothing and yet possessing all things"],[2164.47,"So that's one long sentence."],[2167.88,"But we'll we'll go through it now more slowly."],[2170.92,"Now, first thing in verse three, we give no offense in anything that our ministry may not be blamed."],[2176.28,"Okay. This means something different to us today than it meant then."],[2182.36,"When we think about giving offense, or causing someone to stumble or scandalizing someone, any of that biblical language, we tend to think about people getting offended."],[2195.03,"And so if Saint Paul were living today, we would say, good luck not offending anybody."],[2200.71,"At least in the United States today"],[2204.21,"It is impossible to say more than a couple of words without offending someone."],[2211.09,"You say something nice to one person, there's someone else who is not gonna be happy about it."],[2216.91,"So that's not what it means."],[2219.41,"That's not what it means."],[2221.09,"Being a stumbling box, causing someone to stumble, being a stumbling box, scandalizing someone, giving offense, it means causing to offend."],[2230.37,"It means being a cause for someone to sin."],[2234.61,"That's very different."],[2236.35,"It means causing people to stumble."],[2238.51,"This is related to what he talked about in 1 Corinthians with the weaker brother that we talked about."],[2240.99,"the weaker brother. And in that context, we talked about is not a person who gets offended because you do something"],[2249.49,"It's someone who you doing something might cause them to fall into sin."],[2256.06,"So I think one of the examples we gave at that time, was like there's a difference between having a beer in front of someone who just thinks Christians shouldn't drink beer and having a beer in front of someone who's a recovering alcoholic."],[2272.13,"One of those is maybe offending somebody."],[2275.79,"That's not what St."],[2276.83,"Paul is worried about."],[2278.83,"Okay. A lot of the Pharisees were offended that he ate with Gentiles."],[2283.23,"He didn't care that they were offended"],[2286.93,"A lot of people were offended that Jesus ate with tax collectors and sinners."],[2290.61,"He didn't care that they were offended."],[2292.85,"Okay. But the other one."],[2295.74,"If you drink a beer in front of someone who's a recovering alcoholic, causing temptation for them that might lead them back into the sinful pattern, might lead to their destruction."],[2305.5,"That's a big problem."],[2307.84,"And that's sinning ourselves in terms of not loving that person."],[2313.94,"And so what St."],[2314.82,"Paul is saying here is that he's careful in his ministry to not do anything that's going to lead someone that might lead someone into sin."],[2327.79,"So that, as he says, his ministry is not blamed."],[2334.21,"So that people don't look at Saint Paul and what he's preaching and say, well, look at this bad fruit, that's being born by this tree."],[2345.04,"Look at how this person has gone and lived because of what St."],[2348.32,"Paul told him."],[2351.54,"So he never wants that to happen."],[2353.46,"So it's not only words, but actions."],[2356.66,"So we should not be setting a bad example, but leads people to follow our bad example."],[2363.16,"Right. And it's and it's not just a question of whether we're sinning."],[2367.88,"It's about whether seeing us might lead someone else into sin."],[2369.88,"I guess that's a person"],[2373.42,"Oh, he's a Christian, he's doing this."],[2377.2,"And maybe you're only doing this much in their minds."],[2379.92,"It's a very good thing."],[2380.93,"Or St. Paul saying, well, this particular Jewish custom or something."],[2389.67,"I understand that that applies differently now."],[2393.05,"But he's not going around like what running into synagogues and saying, hey everybody, it's bacon time."],[2402.79,"He's he's not trying to do anything that's gonna, you know."],[2410.0,"Cause offense, cause offenses."],[2412.7,"In that sense."],[2415.9,"And then verse 4, the opposite of that, of doing things that lead to offense is but in all things we commend ourselves as ministers of God."],[2424.02,"Meaning the flip side of that is he wants people to look at his ministry and what he's doing and what he's preaching and see the good fruits that are born by it, the good things that are resulting from it and coming from it."],[2438.84,"And so that's what he is working for."],[2443.48,"Why is he saying that now?"],[2445.73,"He clarified first that it's not that he's taking credit."],[2450.86,"My gospel and the way I I preach it is doing all these good things, so that means'm a great guy."],[2455.06,"He's not taking credit."],[2456.68,"It's God who's doing these things."],[2460.5,"So St. Paul is saying, I work hard to not get in the way."],[2467.16,"I work hard to not block."],[2470.13,"Get in the way, not be an obstacle, to the progress of Christ's gospel in the world."],[2476.53,"But instead to be a coworker, instead to try and do everything he can to facilitate it."],[2481.85,"I like how and be helpful to it."],[2485.17,"Kind of like how Jonah was, I've heard it."],[2488.29,"Yeah, Jonah would be the opposite."],[2491.35,"He did not want."],[2492.63,"He was mad about that"],[2493.25,"And then even when the people repented of Nineveh."],[2499.62,"So yeah, Jonah would be an example of the opposite."],[2501.94,"St. Paul's trying to say he's trying to be the opposite of that."],[2505.0,"To not get in the way, to not right resist and be stubborn."],[2512.44,"And so he gives these examples."],[2514.78,"That he's struggling to do that through being patient in tribulations."],[2522.64,"Trouble, distress, in needs."],[2526.3,"St. Paul wasn't always getting three square meals a day."],[2530.46,"He wasn't wearing nice fancy clothes."],[2533.38,"He was going through need and hardship and distresses in stripes."],[2537.68,"That's getting beaten."],[2540.08,"Beaten with whips, beaten with rods, depending on your Roman city and who is doing the beating."],[2547.84,"In imprisonments, in tumults, in labors and sleeplessness and fastings."],[2553.84,"Okay? So in all these circumstances, he's just listed."],[2557.42,"He's working to be faithful and still try to participate in and cooperate with, do everything he can to promote what God is doing in all these negative circumstances."],[2569.42,"Which again, he's reminding them of because he's look, he knows that if they really get on board, it's not going to be easy."],[2577.28,"He's not saying to them, hey, if you just cooperate with God, you'd be rich and successful and have three cars and everything would go wonderful for you."],[2587.82,"All the troubles you're having are because you're not on board with God's will."],[2591.26,"He's saying the opposite."],[2594.91,"He's saying you need to get on board with God's will because that's how you'll find salvation."],[2598.91,"But it's gonna be tough."],[2601.57,"He's saying it's been tough for me, I know."],[2603.75,"And it's gonna be tough for you too."],[2608.23,"Now he shifts, he shifts his preposition from in, which was the different circumstances, to by."],[2614.85,"So this is how he's trying to work to further. what God is doing"],[2622.81,"By purity, by knowledge, by long suffering, which is another word for patience, by kindness, by the Holy Spirit, by sincere love, by the word of truth, by the power of God, by the armor of righteousness on the right hand and on the left, by honor and dishonor, by evil report and good report."],[2645.29,"Okay, so we'll go through those more slowly again."],[2647.45,"But these are the means."],[2648.81,"This is the how."],[2650.46,"So how? You'll notice some of these are fruits of the spirit."],[2654.5,"So by purity, by trying to maintain his own purity."],[2659.2,"This is part of both participating in what God is doing and not being an obstacle to it."],[2663.2,"ing and Because if he's liv a life of impurity he's the one going around preaching the gospel, that's going to be a hindrance, not a help."],[2675.03,"By knowledge. That doesn't mean, hey, I know a lot of stuff."],[2679.97,"That means he's trying to progress in knowledge."],[2683.26,"St. Paul didn't sort of master the, I mastered the scriptures as a rabbi, and so now I'm good to go."],[2689.92,"He's continuing to learn."],[2694.8,"By patience in all those circumstances he just talked about."],[2699.68,"By kindness. So he's trying by trying to show kindness to everyone, which he's been trying to show to them."],[2707.8,"Things went really badly."],[2711.21,"But as he writes this letter, he hasn't chided them."],[2714.81,"He hasn't yelled at them."],[2716.89,"He hasn't said, How dare you treat me like that?"],[2718.97,"Don't you know I'm an apostle?"],[2720.57,"You need to listen to me and obey."],[2722.47,"None of that."],[2724.41,"It's by kindness, by the Holy Spirit, who's dwelling within him and strengthening him through all this."],[2732.09,"By sincere love that he has for them."],[2738.81,"By the word of truth, by the power of God."],[2741.94,"That's in the gospel that He's that He's proclaiming to them."],[2746.66,"By the armor of righteousness, on the right hand and on the left"],[2750.76,"Armor protects you."],[2753.18,"And so the armor of righteousness that he's talking about is remember he's just talking about us becoming the righteousness of God."],[2759.84,"That we're set right, that we're made right by Christ, and that defends us."],[2766.32,"He's going to get more directly into spiritual warfare type topics in a little bit."],[2770.42,"But he's already alluding to that here."],[2772.59,"Because he and the on the right hand of the left means he's getting attacked from all directions."],[2777.97,"Spiritually. But from whatever direction it comes, he's protected."],[2783.37,"By the by the righteousness of Christ."],[2788.81,"By honor and dishonor."],[2791.27,"Now this is a juxtaposition."],[2794.56,"So by honor."],[2797.34,"Meaning by living his life in an honorable way."],[2801.6,"That helps what he's doing and causes it not to be a hindrance."],[2805.74,"But by continuing to do what he's doing, even when he's dishonored, even when he's shamed, even when he's in these bad situations, he's thrown in prison, he's being beaten, he's being rejected, he stays steadfast."],[2817.84,"So whether by honor or by dishonor, he's still staying the course."],[2825.04,"By evil report and good report, the same thing."],[2829.81,"The same thing."],[2831.01,"Sometimes having certain people hate you does more for your reputation than having them love you."],[2841.63,"Sometimes you look at someone and there's certain people saying bad things about them, and you say, well, if they don't like him, he must be doing something right."],[2850.29,"So that's what he's talking about by evil report and good report."],[2854.31,"Who it is who's slandering him and who it is who's who's giving him the good report."],[2858.63,"Both actually help."],[2861.27,"In terms of what he's doing."],[2864.07,"Listen next time as Father Stephen DeYoung continues his study of the scriptures on the Whole Counsel of God."],[2871.43,"Father Stephen's email address is wholecounsel at ancientfaith.com."],[2874.15,"unsel at That's wholeco ancientfaith.com."]],"o":[{"t":20.88,"lv":2,"h":"Recap: where we are in 2 Corinthians","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\">Picking up at <b>2 Corinthians 6:1</b></li><li class=\"d0\">Paul's <b>fourth letter</b> (at least) to Corinth</li><li class=\"d1\">2 Cor probably <b>several letters</b> put together</li><li class=\"d1\">written after a <b>visit</b> and a letter that <b>\"did not go so well\"</b></li><li class=\"d1\">Corinth still has lots of problems; things got <b>\"very messy\"</b></li><li class=\"d0\">Main theme: <b>reconciliation</b></li><li class=\"d1\">primarily reconciled <b>with each other</b>, back together as <b>one church</b></li><li class=\"d1\">not that he's mad or offended at anyone</li><li class=\"d0\">Ch. 5 developed 1 Corinthians themes</li><li class=\"d1\"><b>gifts and capacities</b> God has given</li><li class=\"d1\">Christ's return and <b>last judgment</b></li><li class=\"d1\">gifts bring <b>accountability and responsibility</b> for how we use them</li></ul>"},{"t":174.92,"lv":2,"h":"6:1 - Workers together with Him","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\">\"We then, as <b>workers together with Him</b>, plead with you not to receive the grace of God <b>in vain</b>\"</li><li class=\"d1\">more important than it looks - bears on <b>modern Protestant beliefs</b> this verse contradicts</li><li class=\"d0\">Workers together = <i>sunergoi</i></li><li class=\"d1\">root of <b>synergy / synergism</b></li><li class=\"d0\">\"with Him\" is in italics - added</li><li class=\"d1\">co-workers must be with someone → previous section is about <b>Christ</b> → co-workers with Christ</li><li class=\"d0\">Plea not to receive grace in vain → it is <b>possible</b> to receive grace in vain</li><li class=\"d1\">Calvinist friends deny it: <b>irresistible grace</b>, grace is <b>monergistic</b> (only God works)</li><li class=\"d1\">Paul uses the word for <b>synergism</b>, not monergism - working together is <b>necessary</b></li></ul>"},{"t":365.06,"lv":3,"h":"Which grace is this?","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\">Objection: just <b>common grace</b> (life, good things for everyone)?</li><li class=\"d1\">but <b>5:21</b> just before: \"made Him who knew no sin to be sin for us\"</li><li class=\"d1\">that's Christ's death and resurrection = our <b>salvation</b></li><li class=\"d0\">Chapter number 6 isn't in the original - <b>no break</b> in what Paul wrote</li><li class=\"d0\">So it's the grace he was just describing</li><li class=\"d1\">Christ already did it - \"a couple thousand years before I was born\"</li><li class=\"d1\">I receive its benefits by grace</li><li class=\"d0\">If I don't <b>cooperate</b> (Latin: <i>co</i> + <i>operate</i>) → receive it <b>in vain</b></li><li class=\"d1\">vain = <b>empty</b>, comes to nothing, does nothing</li></ul>"},{"t":505.11,"lv":2,"h":"Christ acts first; the Exodus pattern","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\">Key to Paul's whole theology - covered back in <b>Romans</b></li><li class=\"d0\">Christ did what He did; <b>we did nothing</b> to get Him to die for us</li><li class=\"d0\">Countering the <b>Pharisee</b> view (Paul was one)</li><li class=\"d1\">got into the mess by disobeying <b>Torah</b> → obey it perfectly and God sends Messiah to rescue</li><li class=\"d1\">Paul: Christ acted <b>\"at just the right time while we were still sinners\"</b></li><li class=\"d0\">Same as the <b>Exodus</b></li><li class=\"d1\">Israelites weren't slaves who started obeying and so <b>earned</b> rescue and land</li><li class=\"d1\">they were <b>sinful and wicked</b>, most died in the desert - <b>God did it</b></li><li class=\"d0\">Christ defeated <b>death</b> and the <b>devil</b>, purified the world from sin - before any of us were born</li><li class=\"d0\">But for it to be meaningful for us, <b>cooperation</b> required</li><li class=\"d1\">not earning - God working <b>in and through us</b>, we don't resist or rebel</li></ul>"},{"t":648.73,"lv":3,"h":"Wilderness generation as warning","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\">Those who died in the desert: resisted, <b>rebelled and grumbled</b></li><li class=\"d1\">went after Moses: \"We had it better in <b>Egypt</b>\"</li><li class=\"d1\">destroyed themselves by resisting</li><li class=\"d0\">God still brought them out → they <b>received</b> the grace, set free</li><li class=\"d1\">but it <b>amounted to nothing</b></li><li class=\"d0\">Same dynamic possible for the <b>Corinthians</b></li><li class=\"d1\"><b>baptized</b> like Israel into Moses in sea and cloud (1 Cor)</li><li class=\"d1\">received the <b>Holy Spirit</b>, in the church, hearing the word</li><li class=\"d1\">but if they <b>harden their hearts</b> → may not make it to the promised land</li><li class=\"d0\">\"Once saved always saved\" - Paul <b>never says that</b></li><li class=\"d0\">Not God as <b>referee</b> grading how you work out your salvation</li><li class=\"d1\">using gifts rightly = <b>cooperating</b> with what God is doing, not independent</li></ul>"},{"t":808.25,"lv":2,"h":"Orthodox view of grace and good works","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\">Crucial to how the Church understands <b>good works</b></li><li class=\"d0\">Debates: Roman Catholic vs. Protestant - faith? faith and works? merit?</li><li class=\"d0\">Orthodox: grace = the <b>energies of God</b></li><li class=\"d1\">not \"sci-fi\" sense - <i>en</i> + <i>erg</i> as in <b>syn-ergy</b> = working</li><li class=\"d1\">God working in and through creation to bring it to <b>perfection</b></li><li class=\"d1\"><b>transfigure</b>, transform, continuously</li><li class=\"d0\">Two options: be <b>co-workers</b> (ourselves and the world) or <b>rebel and resist</b></li><li class=\"d1\">resisting doesn't stop Him getting it done → we <b>destroy ourselves</b>, opt out, are removed</li><li class=\"d1\">explains imagery of the condemned: <b>outside</b> the kingdom, shut out, \"dark place outside\" - they opted out</li></ul>"},{"t":958.56,"lv":2,"h":"Analogy: the realtor","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\">Analogy (imperfect): <b>buying a house</b> through a realtor</li><li class=\"d1\">realtor negotiates, makes offers, signs papers</li><li class=\"d1\">but <b>I</b> pay the money and receive the house - I'm the buyer</li><li class=\"d0\">Paul elsewhere: God has <b>good works prepared in advance</b> for us</li><li class=\"d0\">Church service: I walk to the altar, preach, break the bread, pour the wine</li><li class=\"d1\">but <b>Christ</b> is the one communicating Himself</li><li class=\"d0\">Telling someone the gospel: <b>you</b> speak, but if they're saved <b>Christ saved them</b></li><li class=\"d1\">\"can't take credit\" - realtor can't say \"I bought five houses today\"</li><li class=\"d0\">Other reason it fits: realtor gets a <b>commission</b></li><li class=\"d1\">we're <b>transformed and changed</b> by participating - part of finding salvation</li><li class=\"d1\">yet even the commission comes from me → our changes come from <b>God</b></li></ul>"},{"t":1161.89,"lv":3,"h":"Why God calls them good","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\">God can call the works <b>good</b> because they're <b>His</b></li><li class=\"d1\">like creation: \"it's good\" because <b>He</b> did it</li><li class=\"d1\">not good in the sense of perfect if it's mine</li><li class=\"d0\">If I'd refused, He'd have done it another way → I'd have <b>lost the benefit</b></li><li class=\"d0\">My choice <b>earns nothing</b></li><li class=\"d1\">only whether I <b>exclude myself</b> from God's grace</li><li class=\"d0\">Theme all through these chapters (began with prayer)</li><li class=\"d1\">God is doing it in you, your community, the world → <b>be reconciled</b> to Him and each other</li><li class=\"d1\">resist → <b>cut off</b>; grace already received comes to nothing</li></ul>"},{"t":1279.58,"lv":2,"h":"Significance without boasting; both sides","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\">Comment: gives <b>significance</b> to actions without reason to be boastful</li><li class=\"d1\">\"nothing to brag about, but our actions are incredibly significant\"</li><li class=\"d0\">God calling us to do these things = a <b>gift</b> we accept or refuse</li><li class=\"d0\">Flip side of \"be reconciled\"</li><li class=\"d1\">community must <b>forgive</b> those who return</li><li class=\"d1\">returners must be <b>willing</b> to return, not harden hearts</li><li class=\"d1\">\"That community was mean to me with the discipline, so I'm done\"</li><li class=\"d0\">Paul presses <b>both</b>: those separated - come back; those in - receive them back</li><li class=\"d0\">Staying away keeps cutting you off from what God wants to do through you <b>personally and as a community</b></li></ul>"},{"t":1375.52,"lv":2,"h":"Q&amp;A: recognizing when we frustrate grace","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\">Q: does Paul say how to <b>recognize</b> early that you're frustrating grace?</li><li class=\"d0\">A: he'll come back to it, practically</li><li class=\"d1\">also: <b>never too late</b></li><li class=\"d1\">hardened heart for three years → <b>tomorrow you can soften it</b></li><li class=\"d0\">Q: how do we know what God is doing and how to participate?</li><li class=\"d1\">first: the <b>gospel itself</b> proclaims what God is doing</li><li class=\"d1\"><b>5:21</b>: Christ made sin for us; \"God is in Christ <b>reconciling the whole world</b> to Himself\"</li><li class=\"d0\"><b>1 Corinthians 13</b>: love of God comes to us; we cooperate by loving</li><li class=\"d1\">my love is human, fragile, tainted; <b>God loving you through me</b> = perfect</li><li class=\"d1\">I'm transformed in the process</li><li class=\"d0\">Matthew's <b>sick and prisoners</b> = expressing God's love</li></ul>"},{"t":1541.38,"lv":2,"h":"Commandments as guide to God's will","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\">How Paul understands the <b>commandments and Torah</b></li><li class=\"d1\">\"he who does these things will find <b>life</b> in them\"</li><li class=\"d0\">Commandments = <b>guide to what God is doing</b>, to His will in the world</li><li class=\"d1\">following them = participating</li><li class=\"d1\"><b>Leviticus</b>: love your neighbor as yourself → part of what God does → transformative, gives life</li><li class=\"d0\">Coming in a few seconds: <b>holiness</b></li><li class=\"d1\">many commandments: avoid filthy and unclean, stay <b>separate</b>, keep purity</li><li class=\"d1\">God is holy and is making creation holy by <b>purifying</b> it</li><li class=\"d0\">All commandments of both Testaments, rightly understood, = <b>guide to God's will</b></li></ul>"},{"t":1657.81,"lv":3,"h":"Decisions: plumber or carpenter","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\">Contrast with modern talk of <b>figuring out God's will</b></li><li class=\"d1\">should I marry this person? take this career?</li><li class=\"d0\">Unless it's <b>sinful</b> (running a brothel or casino) - commandments tell us</li><li class=\"d0\">Carpenter or plumber? <b>you get to choose</b></li><li class=\"d1\">good news and bad news - can't throw the <b>Urim and Thummim</b> and opt out</li><li class=\"d0\"><b>Wisdom</b> needed: ramifications</li><li class=\"d1\">nothing sinful in being a lawyer, but some <b>types of law</b> a Christian can't do</li><li class=\"d1\">\"this jurisdiction, this office, this person\"</li><li class=\"d0\">God has no will about <b>which cereal</b> - \"Apple Jacks or Sugar Crisp\"</li><li class=\"d1\">no minutiae where wrong choice = trouble (against <b>extreme Calvinists</b>)</li><li class=\"d0\">God's will = what He's doing; direct link to <b>His energies</b></li><li class=\"d1\">plumber or carpenter: be kind to poor, <b>fruits of the Spirit</b></li></ul>"},{"t":1850.72,"lv":2,"h":"Q&amp;A: living among pagans","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\">Comment: hard when no one around you does this</li><li class=\"d1\">\"exactly the problem they had in <b>Corinth</b>\" - surrounded by pagans</li><li class=\"d0\">Corinthians lived like pagans <b>85-90%</b> of the time, Christian the other 10-15</li><li class=\"d1\">even brought paganism into church - big problem of <b>1 Corinthians</b></li><li class=\"d0\">They had to <b>opt out of everything</b> - more than we do today</li><li class=\"d1\">city <b>feast days</b> = worship of pagan gods</li><li class=\"d1\">craftsmen's <b>guilds</b> had patron gods; meetings included their worship</li><li class=\"d1\">Christian must opt out → <b>very difficult</b> if not in the guild</li><li class=\"d0\">Why Paul lists his <b>shipwrecks and beatings</b></li><li class=\"d1\">not bragging - he knows how hard it is</li><li class=\"d0\">Bad influence works, so does good: Paul quotes <b>Menander</b> - \"bad company corrupts good morals\"</li></ul>"},{"t":2044.25,"lv":2,"h":"6:2 - Now is the day of salvation","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\">\"In an acceptable time I have heard you, and in the day of salvation I have helped you. Behold, <b>now</b> is the accepted time\"</li><li class=\"d0\">Quotes <b>Isaiah</b></li><li class=\"d1\">prophetic: time will come when God acts to <b>save His people</b></li><li class=\"d1\">Paul: \"guess what - <b>that's now</b>\"</li><li class=\"d0\">Ties to earlier point</li><li class=\"d1\">no matter how long you've hardened your heart or resisted</li><li class=\"d1\"><b>today</b> you can find salvation - still \"now\" for us</li><li class=\"d0\">God has <b>done it in Christ</b> → you just need to be <b>reconciled</b></li><li class=\"d0\">Chapter was nearly an episode on its own</li></ul>"},{"t":2111.99,"lv":2,"h":"6:3-10 - Reading the long list","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\">Paul's <b>one long sentence</b>: ministers of God in patience, tribulations, needs, distresses, stripes, imprisonments, tumults, labors, sleeplessness, fastings; by purity, knowledge, long-suffering, kindness, Holy Spirit, sincere love, word of truth, power of God, armor of righteousness; by honor and dishonor, evil report and good report</li><li class=\"d0\">Contrasts: deceivers yet true, unknown yet well known, dying yet live, chastened not killed, sorrowful yet rejoicing, poor yet making many rich, having nothing yet possessing all</li><li class=\"d0\">Going back through <b>more slowly</b></li></ul>"},{"t":2170.92,"lv":2,"h":"6:3 - Giving no offense","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\">\"We give no offense in anything that our ministry may not be blamed\"</li><li class=\"d0\">Means something <b>different</b> now</li><li class=\"d1\">we think of people <b>getting offended</b></li><li class=\"d1\">today \"good luck\" - impossible to say a few words in the U.S. without offending someone</li><li class=\"d0\">Biblical <b>offense / stumbling block / scandalizing</b> = being a <b>cause for someone to sin</b></li><li class=\"d1\">tied to the <b>weaker brother</b> in 1 Corinthians</li><li class=\"d0\">Beer example</li><li class=\"d1\">before one who thinks Christians shouldn't drink: maybe offends - not Paul's concern</li><li class=\"d1\">before a <b>recovering alcoholic</b>: temptation, may lead to destruction - sinning by <b>not loving</b> them</li><li class=\"d0\">Pharisees offended by eating with <b>Gentiles</b>; others by Jesus with <b>tax collectors</b> - He didn't care</li></ul>"},{"t":2327.79,"lv":3,"h":"Not blamed; bad examples","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\">Goal: ministry <b>not blamed</b></li><li class=\"d1\">people don't look at Paul's preaching and say \"look at the <b>bad fruit</b> of this tree\"</li><li class=\"d0\">Not only words but <b>actions</b></li><li class=\"d1\">don't set a bad example others follow</li><li class=\"d1\">not just whether I sin, but whether <b>seeing me</b> leads another into sin</li><li class=\"d0\">Paul not running into synagogues saying <b>\"it's bacon time\"</b></li><li class=\"d1\">avoids causing offense in that sense</li></ul>"},{"t":2415.9,"lv":2,"h":"6:4 - Commending ourselves as ministers","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\">Flip side: wants people to see the <b>good fruits</b> of his ministry</li><li class=\"d0\">Not taking credit - <b>God</b> is doing these things</li><li class=\"d0\">Paul: \"I work hard <b>not to get in the way</b>\"</li><li class=\"d1\">not an <b>obstacle</b> to the gospel's progress</li><li class=\"d1\">be a <b>coworker</b>, facilitate it, be helpful</li><li class=\"d0\">Opposite example: <b>Jonah</b></li><li class=\"d1\">mad even when <b>Nineveh repented</b></li><li class=\"d1\">Paul tries to be the opposite - not resist, not stubborn</li></ul>"},{"t":2514.78,"lv":3,"h":"In: patience in hardships","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\">Preposition <b>\"in\"</b> = circumstances</li><li class=\"d0\">Tribulations, <b>needs</b>, distresses</li><li class=\"d1\">not always three square meals, no fancy clothes</li><li class=\"d0\"><b>Stripes</b> = beaten with whips or rods, depending on Roman city</li><li class=\"d0\">Imprisonments, tumults, labors, sleeplessness, fastings</li><li class=\"d0\">Faithful and cooperating with God <b>in all these negatives</b></li><li class=\"d0\">Reminding them: if they get on board it <b>won't be easy</b></li><li class=\"d1\">not \"cooperate with God and be rich, <b>three cars</b>\"</li><li class=\"d1\">not \"your troubles are because you're not on board\" - the <b>opposite</b></li><li class=\"d1\">get on board because that's how you find <b>salvation</b> - \"tough for me, tough for you\"</li></ul>"},{"t":2608.23,"lv":2,"h":"By: purity, knowledge, kindness","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\">Shifts from <b>in</b> to <b>by</b> = the <b>means</b>, the how</li><li class=\"d0\">Some are <b>fruits of the Spirit</b></li><li class=\"d0\"><b>Purity</b></li><li class=\"d1\">part of participating and not obstructing - impure life while preaching = hindrance</li><li class=\"d0\"><b>Knowledge</b></li><li class=\"d1\">not \"I know a lot\" - he's <b>progressing</b>; didn't just master Scripture as a rabbi</li><li class=\"d0\"><b>Long-suffering</b> = patience, in those circumstances</li><li class=\"d0\"><b>Kindness</b></li><li class=\"d1\">shown to Corinth though things went badly</li><li class=\"d1\">hasn't chided or yelled: \"How dare you? Don't you know I'm an <b>apostle</b>?\" - none of that</li></ul>"},{"t":2724.41,"lv":3,"h":"By: Spirit, love, truth, armor","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\">By the <b>Holy Spirit</b> dwelling in him and strengthening him</li><li class=\"d0\">By <b>sincere love</b> for them</li><li class=\"d0\">By the <b>word of truth</b>, the <b>power of God</b> = the gospel he proclaims</li><li class=\"d0\"><b>Armor of righteousness</b> on right hand and left</li><li class=\"d1\">armor <b>protects</b></li><li class=\"d1\">= becoming the <b>righteousness of God</b>, set right by Christ - defends him</li><li class=\"d1\">hints at <b>spiritual warfare</b>, coming a little later</li><li class=\"d1\">right and left = attacked from <b>all directions</b>, but protected by Christ's righteousness</li></ul>"},{"t":2788.81,"lv":3,"h":"6:8 - Honor and dishonor; evil and good report","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\">Now a <b>juxtaposition</b></li><li class=\"d0\"><b>Honor</b>: living honorably helps, not a hindrance</li><li class=\"d0\"><b>Dishonor</b>: shamed, in prison, beaten, rejected - stays <b>steadfast</b></li><li class=\"d1\">either way, <b>stays the course</b></li><li class=\"d0\"><b>Evil report and good report</b> - same</li><li class=\"d1\">sometimes being hated by certain people helps your reputation more than their love</li><li class=\"d1\">\"if they don't like him, he must be doing something right\"</li><li class=\"d1\">who slanders him and who praises him - <b>both help</b></li></ul>"}]});
